  "summary_en": "NIST's voluntary, sector-agnostic AI Risk Management Framework 1.0. It defines characteristics of trustworthy AI and a Core of four functions (Govern, Map, Measure, Manage) with categories and subcategories, plus profiles. It has no robot-specific provisions and mentions safety only generically.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Voluntary, rights-preserving, use-case-agnostic framework directed by the National AI Initiative Act of 2020",
   "Seven trustworthiness characteristics: valid and reliable, safe, secure and resilient, accountable and transparent, explainable, privacy-enhanced, fair",
   "Core functions Govern, Map, Measure, Manage with subcategory outcomes",
   "Risk prioritization; halt development or deployment when risks are unacceptable",
   "Use-case, temporal and cross-sectoral profiles; living document with review by 2028"
